Source: beerssh
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), qt6-base-dev, qt6-base-dev-tools,
               cmake, libssl-dev, libsecret-1-dev, libsixel-dev,
               zlib1g-dev, libxcb1-dev, pkgconf
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: beerssh
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: beerssh-fonts
Description: SSH terminal for desktop and Android
 An SSH client with a real terminal emulator, built from one
 codebase for the desktop and for Android. Sessions live apart
 from the windows showing them, so tabs, split panes and a phone
 rotating do not disturb a connection.

Package: beerssh-fonts
Architecture: all
Depends: beerssh (>= ${source:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: curated terminal fonts for BeerSSH
 The terminal fonts BeerSSH ships with, each vetted for the
 properties a character grid needs, with their licence texts.
 Without this package BeerSSH uses the system monospace fonts.

Package: beersshd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: SFTP-only server for one folder
 Serves one folder over SFTP, and nothing else, to the keys in an
 authorized keys file and to a password once one is set. It runs
 no shell and no commands, forwards nothing, and keeps every path
 inside the folder. Modern scp works; the legacy scp protocol
 does not. Independent of the BeerSSH terminal.

Package: beerssh-session
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: keeps a shell on a server when the connection drops
 Install this on a server to let BeerSSH keep its shell there: the
 shell goes on running through a dropped connection, and whatever it
 printed meanwhile is there when BeerSSH comes back. Run over SSH by
 BeerSSH, with no daemon and nothing to configure. Linked statically,
 so it depends on nothing.
